  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 147 AM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nWe'll continue to watch the high pressure over the Four Corners and \nwe'll get daily thunderstorms off the high terrain of NM, but \ndepending on the overall upper flow, or if we can get any \ndisturbances embedded will enhance or suppress those storm chances. \nRight now the focus would continue to be the typical areas, like the \nnorthwest Panhandles, but with enough help maybe they extend further \ninto the Panhandles.  There is some hints midweek that maybe the \nupper ridge will brake down from a stronger disturbance to the \nnorth, and that could change quite a bit and expand the area of \nprecipitation chances. But there is certainly a divergence in \nagreement with the long range models as to if we'll still stay \nunder this hot and dry high pressure system, or get a potential \nbreakdown that leads to increased precipitation chances.  So with \nthat the pops in the extended will be about par for the course, \neither dry, or slight chance to chance in the northwest Panhandles. \n\nWeber",
